WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.136
Sign in with a Google account that has been granted access.

00:00:05.136 --> 00:00:06.641
Open Video Studio.

00:00:06.641 --> 00:00:10.322
Choose English or Chinese for the interface.

00:00:10.322 --> 00:00:15.592
Later, choose the output language in your project settings: the

00:00:15.592 --> 00:00:21.531
interface language and the final video's language are separate choices.

00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:29.326
Search Douyin for your topic and select one to five useful reference videos.

00:00:29.326 --> 00:00:35.399
Look for a strong opening, clear explanation, or effective pacing.

00:00:35.399 --> 00:00:41.196
References teach editing techniques; they are not your footage.

00:00:41.196 --> 00:00:45.152
If the analyze button asks for a reference,

00:00:45.152 --> 00:00:48.741
return to step one and select a result.

00:00:49.567 --> 00:00:53.204
Upload the video you want to improve, up

00:00:53.204 --> 00:00:57.661
to seven minutes and two hundred fifty megabytes.

00:00:57.661 --> 00:01:02.390
Name the project and confirm your rights to edit it.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:04.845
Wait for upload completion.

00:01:04.845 --> 00:01:09.210
Saved progress shows bytes stored on the server.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:17.486
If interrupted, follow the resume or retry message rather than creating duplicate projects.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:25.941
In Script and intended message, explain the subject, audience takeaway, and next action.

00:01:25.941 --> 00:01:31.759
For example: tour an apartment in Bangkok; show its layout, natural

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:37.055
light, and kitchen; end with an invitation to book a viewing.

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:41.658
Include exact facts and a full script when available.

00:01:41.658 --> 00:01:48.343
This field guides the edit; it does not automatically create a new voiceover.

00:01:49.167 --> 00:01:55.336
Use Brand rules and claims to avoid for tone and factual limits.

00:01:55.336 --> 00:02:04.109
For example: calm and professional; no invented prices or distances; no guaranteed returns.

00:02:04.109 --> 00:02:09.121
For citizenship content, avoid promises of approval.

00:02:09.121 --> 00:02:12.688
For travel, do not invent visa rules.

00:02:12.688 --> 00:02:15.677
State missing facts explicitly.

00:02:15.677 --> 00:02:22.810
Never present unrelated B-roll as proof of the featured property or place.

00:02:23.633 --> 00:02:29.335
Choose your topic, target audience, tone, and output language.

00:02:29.335 --> 00:02:32.462
Set the project AI spending limit.

00:02:32.462 --> 00:02:39.267
It is a ceiling, not a fixed price; reference search charges are separate.

00:02:39.267 --> 00:02:42.210
Click Analyze and build my plan.

00:02:42.210 --> 00:02:47.543
Wait for the reference analysis and your footage analysis.

00:02:47.543 --> 00:02:54.073
If analysis fails, your saved video does not need to be uploaded again.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:03:00.390
Read the reference DNA to understand the techniques being borrowed.

00:03:00.390 --> 00:03:06.044
Then inspect the proposed Director Timeline against your own footage.

00:03:06.044 --> 00:03:10.796
Each decision should explain what changes, where, and why.

00:03:10.796 --> 00:03:17.270
A reference about another subject must not introduce its facts into your video.

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:23.251
Accept a suitable plan into the editor, then review the individual shots.

00:03:24.067 --> 00:03:25.319
Select a shot.

00:03:25.319 --> 00:03:31.672
Adjust its source range, framing, camera movement, transition, or text.

00:03:31.672 --> 00:03:37.667
Check the timeline layers for graphics, sound effects, and inserts.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:40.530
Approve the shot when satisfied.

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:44.646
Changing its editing settings clears approval.

00:03:44.646 --> 00:03:47.956
Lock a decision you want to preserve.

00:03:47.956 --> 00:03:54.398
Save your plan; only approved shots are included in the rendered output.

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:58.914
Upload licensed clips in Video and music

00:03:58.914 --> 00:04:02.721
library, or use the scene's stock search.

00:04:02.721 --> 00:04:08.199
Import a useful result, then match it to the selected shot.

00:04:08.199 --> 00:04:13.770
AI reviews sampled portions, not every frame of long assets.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:20.455
Preview the proposed insert, replace the decision, and approve it again.

00:04:20.455 --> 00:04:27.511
Generated B-roll is an illustration, not verified news or property evidence.

00:04:28.333 --> 00:04:32.100
Correct caption text and choose its style.

00:04:32.100 --> 00:04:37.661
Use visual cards only with supplied facts and accurate values.

00:04:37.661 --> 00:04:44.477
Upload licensed music, select a track, and adjust volume, fades, or ducking.

00:04:44.477 --> 00:04:47.795
You can request a music suggestion or

00:04:47.795 --> 00:04:51.921
preview safe cuts aligned to detected accents.

00:04:51.921 --> 00:04:58.737
These are estimates: listen to the rendered mix before approving the result.

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:04.256
Save your changes before asking AI for an alternative.

00:05:04.256 --> 00:05:11.030
Select an unlocked shot, choose the task, and describe a specific improvement.

00:05:11.030 --> 00:05:17.630
For example: use a gentle push-in while keeping the speaker's full sentence.

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:21.104
Review the proposal before replacing it.

00:05:21.104 --> 00:05:25.359
No suitable match means the edit stays unchanged.

00:05:25.359 --> 00:05:28.746
Reapprove changed shots and save again.

00:05:29.567 --> 00:05:31.959
Render the approved plan.

00:05:31.959 --> 00:05:36.074
Watch the complete master with sound: check

00:05:36.074 --> 00:05:41.147
cuts, words, subtitles, overlays, and factual claims.

00:05:41.147 --> 00:05:48.612
Optional AI review scores five editorial categories and may draft corrections.

00:05:48.612 --> 00:05:52.918
A proposed fix is not a verified improvement.

00:05:52.918 --> 00:05:57.512
Read any reasons a correction could not be made.

00:05:57.512 --> 00:06:05.838
After changing the plan, render again; an existing video does not update automatically.

00:06:06.667 --> 00:06:11.446
After reviewing the master, prepare the platform package.

00:06:11.446 --> 00:06:16.393
Check the duration, aspect ratio, opening, captions, cover,

00:06:16.393 --> 00:06:19.411
and call to action for each version.

00:06:19.411 --> 00:06:22.765
Review and lock the versions you accept.

00:06:22.765 --> 00:06:25.784
Download the video and export files.

00:06:25.784 --> 00:06:30.898
Lumen does not publish to your social accounts automatically.

00:06:30.898 --> 00:06:35.342
You make the final editorial and publishing decision.

